# Boswas OS v1 - application compatibility and isolation
#
# Wine 10.0 (Debian 13). 64-bit and 32-bit Windows applications (ADR-0022):
# Debian 13's wine64 contains only 64-bit Windows modules (no new-style
# WoW64), so 32-bit programs need wine32 from the i386 architecture. The
# ":i386" suffix makes live-build enable i386 as a dpkg foreign architecture
# (multiarch) before installing: 32-bit libraries next to the amd64 system,
# which stays a 64-bit operating system (amd64 kernel, amd64 userland).
# Flatpak is installed without any remote configured: an approved remote is
# enabled only by an administrator (boswas-sysops flatpak-remote-enable).
# libfuse2t64: FUSE 2 library for AppImages built with the older runtime.

wine
wine64
wine32:i386
flatpak
bubblewrap
libfuse2t64
